# The lab's resolver, "behind the hubs" on the internal network. It answers
# the two names the targets have, so that a dynamic access list
# (docs/ACL.md) has something to resolve, and forwards everything else
# upstream, the way the resolver of a real network does. The hubs believe it
# because their config names it in dns_learn_from, and the hubs offer it to
# their spokes (`dns:`), so a spoke that points its host at it keeps working
# for every other name as well -- which matters on a laptop that joins the
# lab while its user is reading mail.
.:53 {
    hosts {
        10.60.0.10 target.lab
        10.60.0.11 tls.lab
        fallthrough
    }
    forward . /etc/resolv.conf
    errors
}
